# {{name}}

A long-running agent app on `@theokit/host`. `main.mjs` is the entry; `app.mjs` declares the config file.

```sh
npm install
node main.mjs onboard --yes   # writes the config file (omit --yes to be asked)
node main.mjs                 # runs; SIGINT or SIGTERM stops it cleanly
node main.mjs daemon install  # login service (systemd --user, launchd, Task Scheduler)
node main.mjs daemon status   # exit 0 running, 3 otherwise
node main.mjs daemon restart
node main.mjs daemon logs --lines 100
node main.mjs daemon uninstall
```

The service registered in `main.mjs` is a placeholder; replace it with your agent workload.

## Container

```sh
docker build -t {{name}} .
docker run --rm -v {{name}}-data:/data {{name}} onboard --yes
docker run -d -v {{name}}-data:/data {{name}}
```

`/data` holds `config/`, `state/` and logs, and is the only volume. The image runs as the non-root `node` user (uid 1000); a bind-mounted directory must be writable by it.
